From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] verify_qdisc: check cake_mq on a device with several queues

cake_mq refuses a device with one transmit queue, and verify_qdisc's
throwaway ifb has one unless USE_MQ is on. USE_MQ_EGRESS (patch 100) can be
on with USE_MQ off: select_cake's check for the interface's own qdisc then
always failed, so the upload never got cake_mq, and logged an error. The
check uses an ifb with two queues; select_cake still requires the real
device to have more than one.

diff --git a/src/functions.sh b/src/functions.sh
index 52c3b95..0cc6791 100644
--- a/src/functions.sh
+++ b/src/functions.sh
@@ -345,7 +345,14 @@ verify_qdisc() {
         done
         [ "$found" -eq "1" ] || return 1
     fi
-    create_ifb $ifb || return 1
+    if [ "$qdisc" = "cake_mq" ]; then
+        # cake_mq only works on a device with several transmit queues; the
+        # ifb create_ifb makes has one unless USE_MQ is on, which is for the
+        # download alone (USE_MQ_EGRESS can be on without it)
+        $IP link add name $ifb numtxqueues 2 type ifb || return 1
+    else
+        create_ifb $ifb || return 1
+    fi
 
 
     case $qdisc in
